BLE_MODE_CENTRAL|Custom P2P Client|BLE Services Configuration||||
BLE_MODE_PERIPHERAL_CENTRAL|Custom P2P Router|BLE Services Configuration||||
SYSTICK_SOURCE_CLOCK_SELECTION|Systick Source Clock Selection|BLE Wireless Stack||||
USER_GUIDANCE|Application configuration recommendations|Application configuration - Project IP's Configuration||||<font color="blue"><b>In Project Manager, Advanced Settings panel:</b></font><> <font color="blue">   • Generate Code shall be unticked for TIM16.</font><> <font color="blue">   • Do Not Generate Function Call shall be unticked for all IP's associated to STM32WPAN configuration excepted for UART, ADC, TIM16 and CRC.</font><> <font color="blue">   • Visibility Static shall be unticked for all IP's associated to STM32WPAN configuration excepted for SystemPower_Config an TIM16.</font><> <font color="blue">   • Register CallBack shall be enabled for UART.</font><> <!-- <font color="blue">   • Generate Code shall be unticked for CRC if USE_SNVMA_NVM is set to YES as the CRC_Ctrl is used to manage the ressource.</font><> --> <!-- <font color="blue">   • Generate Code shall be unticked for ADC if USE_TEMPERATURE_BASED_RADIO_CALIBRATION is set to YES as the ADC_Ctrl is used to manage the ressource.</font><> --> <font color="blue"><b>In case of TZ=1 project:</b></font><> <font color="blue">   • GPIO OSC_OUT pin assignment shall be set to Cortex-M33 no secure</font><> <font color="blue">   • RTC full secure, located in RTC Security panel shall be disabled</font><>
CFG_TX_POWER|CFG_TX_POWER|Application configuration - Application parameters||||
CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME|CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME|Application configuration - Application parameters||||GAP device name
CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME_LENGTH|CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME_LENGTH|Application configuration - Application parameters||1|48|GAP device name lenght; max value is 48bytes.
CFG_BD_ADDRESS|CFG_BD_ADDRESS|Application configuration - Application parameters||0x000000000000|0xFFFFFFFFFFFF|e.g. 0x0008E12A1234, When entering 0x0 the BD address will be genarated based on Unique Device Number.
CFG_BD_ADDRESS_DEVICE|Device Address Type|Application configuration - Application parameters||||List of device address types, used in aci_gap_set_authentication_requirement, possible values: - Public address(PUBLIC_ADDR 0) - Static Random address (STATIC_RANDOM_ADDR 1); if you activate RNG then you will get the choice between STATIC and DYNAMIC Random address
CFG_BD_ADDRESS_TYPE|Private Address Type|Application configuration - Application parameters||||List of own address types, used for advertise, scan or connect. Possible values: - Resolvable private address (GAP_RESOLVABLE_PRIVATE_ADDR 2) - Non resolvable private address(GAP_NON_RESOLVABLE_PRIVATE_ADDR 3)
CFG_STATIC_RANDOM_ADDRESS|RANDOM_ADDRESS type|Application configuration - Application parameters||||List of random address types, can be: - Static, Random Address is fixed for lifetime of the device - Dynamic, Random Address is generated with the RNG at each bootup.
STATIC_RANDOM_ADDRESS|STATIC_RANDOM_ADDRESS|Application configuration - Application parameters||0x000000000000|0xFFFFFFFFFFFF|e.g. 0x0008E12A1234
CFG_PRIVACY|CFG_PRIVACY|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Privacy option
CFG_RNG|RNG status|Advertising configuration||||
CFG_GAP_APPEARANCE|CFG_GAP_APPEARANCE|Application configuration - Application parameters||||GAP appearance selection
CFG_PHY_PREF|CFG_PHY_PREF|Application configuration - Application parameters||||PHY preference selection
CFG_PHY_PREF_TX|CFG_PHY_PREF_TX|Application configuration - Application parameters||||
CFG_PHY_PREF_RX|CFG_PHY_PREF_RX|Application configuration - Application parameters||||
CFG_HW_RNG_POOL_SIZE|CFG_HW_RNG_POOL_SIZE|Application configuration - Application parameters||1|256|Size of pool buffer of random numbers
CFG_HW_RNG_POOL_THRESHOLD|CFG_HW_RNG_POOL_THRESHOLD|Application configuration - Application parameters||10|256|Threshold of random numbers available before triggering pool refill
PKA_INTR_PRIO|PKA_INTR_PRIO|Application configuration - Application parameters||7|13|PKA Interrupt priority
CFG_BLE_NUM_CLIENT_CONTEXTS|CFG_BLE_NUM_CLIENT_CONTEXTS|Application configuration - Application parameters||1|20|Maximum number of Client contexts. One context is used for each connected server.
CFG_BONDING_MODE|CFG_BONDING_MODE|Application configuration - BLE security||||Define Bonding modes Possible values: - No-bonding mode(0x00) - Bonding mode(0x01)
CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MAX|CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MAX|Application configuration - BLE security||=CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|16|Encryption key maximum size
CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|Application configuration - BLE security||7|16|Encryption key minimum size
CFG_IO_CAPABILITY|CFG_IO_CAPABILITY|Application configuration - BLE security||||Define IO capabilities
CFG_MITM_PROTECTION|CFG_MITM_PROTECTION|Application configuration - BLE security||||Activate/deactivate Define Man In The Middle(MITM) protection mode Possible values: - MITM protection not required (0x00) - MITM protection required (0x01)
CFG_SC_SUPPORT|CFG_SC_SUPPORT|Application configuration - BLE security||||Define Secure Connections Support Possible values: - Secure Connections Paring not supported (0x00) - Secure Connections Paring supported but optional (0x01) - Secure Connections Paring supported and mandatory(0x02)
CFG_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATION_SUPPORT|CFG_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATION_SUPPORT|Application configuration - BLE security||||Define Keypress notification support
CFG_BLE_IR|CFG_BLE_IR|Application configuration - BLE security||||Identity root key (16 bytes) used to derive IRK and DHK(Legacy) When entering 0x0 for all the 16 bytes, the key will be generated based on Unique Device Identifier.
CFG_BLE_IR_HEX|CFG_BLE_IR_HEX|Application configuration - BLE security||||Identity root key (16 bytes) used to derive IRK and DHK(Legacy) When entering 0x0 for all the 16 bytes, the key will be generated based on Unique Device Identifier.
CFG_BLE_ER|CFG_BLE_ER|Application configuration - BLE security||||Encryption root key (16 bytes) used to derive LTK and CSRK When entering 0x0 for all the 16 bytes, the key will be generated based on Unique Device Identifier.
CFG_BLE_ER_HEX|CFG_BLE_ER_HEX|Application configuration - BLE security||||Encryption root key (16 bytes) used to derive LTK and CSRK When entering 0x0 for all the 16 bytes, the key will be generated based on Unique Device Identifier.
BLE_STACK_TYPE|BLE_STACK_TYPE|Application configuration - BLE stack||||BLE_STACK_TYPE_FULL: BLE stack with all features available In LL_ONLY mode, allows to select the link layer variant.
CFG_BLE_NUM_LINK|CFG_BLE_NUM_LINK|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|20|Maximum number of simultaneous connections that the device will support, limited to 8 with BLE Full and Peripheral Only stacks.
CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_SERVICES|CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_SERVICES|Application configuration - BLE stack||2||Maximum number of Services that can be stored in the GATT database Maximum value depends on Gatt database size allocated Note that the GAP and GATT services are automatically added so this parameter should be 2 plus the number of user services
CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_ATTRIBUTES|CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_ATTRIBUTES|Application configuration - BLE stack||9||Maximum number of Attributes (i.e. the number of characteristic + the number of characteristic values + the number of descriptors, excluding the services) that can be stored in the GATT database. Maximum value depends on Gatt database size allocated Note that certain characteristics and relative descriptors are added automatically during device initialization
CFG_BLE_ATT_MTU_MAX|CFG_BLE_ATT_MTU_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||23|512|Maximum supported ATT_MTU size
CFG_BLE_ATT_VALUE_ARRAY_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ATT_VALUE_ARRAY_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|65535|Size of the storage area for Attribute values This value depends on the number of attributes used by application. In particular the sum of the following quantities (in octets) should be made for each attribute: - attribute value length - 5, if UUID is 16 bit; 19, if UUID is 128 bit - 2, if server configuration descriptor is used - 2*DTM_NUM_LINK, if client configuration descriptor is used - 2, if extended properties is used The total amount of memory needed is the sum of the above quantities for each attribute.
CFG_BLE_EATT_BEARER_PER_LINK|CFG_BLE_EATT_BEARER_PER_LINK|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|64|Maximum number of bearers that can be created for Enhanced ATT per ACL links
CFG_BLE_ATTR_PREPARE_WRITE_VALUE_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ATTR_PREPARE_WRITE_VALUE_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Value defined by the formula DIVC(max_char_size, default_att_mtu - 5) * 2 max_char_size: Maximum characteristic’s value size default_att_mtu = 23
CFG_BLE_MBLOCK_COUNT_MARGIN|CFG_BLE_MBLOCK_COUNT_MARGIN|Application configuration - BLE stack||0x0|0xFF|The memory margin to take regarding the number of allocated memory blocks for the BLE stack.
CFG_BLE_HOST_EVENT_BUF_SIZE|CFG_BLE_HOST_EVENT_BUF_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|4096|Amount of memory allocated for BLE host events in bytes. Can be set to 0 to not use it.
CFG_BLE_COC_NBR_MAX|CFG_BLE_COC_NBR_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|64|Maximum number of the connection-oriented channel
CFG_BLE_COC_MPS_MAX|CFG_BLE_COC_MPS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||23|248|Maximum value of the connection-oriented channel Maximum Payload Size
CFG_BLE_COC_INITIATOR_NBR_MAX|CFG_BLE_COC_INITIATOR_NBR_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|=CFG_BLE_COC_NBR_MAX|Maximum number of connection-oriented channels in initiator mode
CFG_BLE_EXTRA_DATA_BUF_SIZE|CFG_BLE_EXTRA_DATA_BUF_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|4096|Size of the RAM buffer allocated for the extension of Host commands
CFG_BLE_LONG_WRITE_DATA_BUF_SIZE|CFG_BLE_LONG_WRITE_DATA_BUF_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Size of the RAM buffer allocated for long write commands
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS|CFG_BLE_OPTIONS|Application configuration - BLE stack||||BLE stack options bitmap, unspecified bits are reserved and shall be set to 0.
BLE_OPTIONS_LL_ONLY|- BLE_OPTIONS_LL_ONLY|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Link Layer option selection (bit 0)
BLE_OPTIONS_NO_SVC_CHANGE_DESC|- BLE_OPTIONS_NO_SVC_CHANGE_DESC|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Service changed descriptor option selection (bit 1)
BLE_OPTIONS_DEV_NAME_READ_ONLY|- BLE_OPTIONS_DEV_NAME_READ_ONLY|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Devive name property option selection (bit 2)
BLE_OPTIONS_EXTENDED_ADV|- BLE_OPTIONS_EXTENDED_ADV|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Extended advertising option selection (bit 3). Available only with full stack.
BLE_OPTIONS_REDUCED_DB_IN_NVM|- BLE_OPTIONS_REDUCED_DB_IN_NVM|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Reduced database in Non Volatile Memory option selection (bit 5)
BLE_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING|- BLE_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING|Application configuration - BLE stack||||GATT caching option selection (bit 6)
BLE_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS_1|- BLE_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS_1|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Power class option selection (bit 7)
BLE_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE_WRITABLE|- BLE_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE_WRITABLE|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Appearance property option selection (bit 8)
BLE_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT|- BLE_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Enhanced ATTribute option selection (bit 9)
BLE_AUDIO_LIB|BLE_AUDIO_LIB|Application configuration - BLE audio||||Add BLE audio libraries to project, refer to BLE Audio applications from STM32CubeWBA firmware package for usage
CFG_SCM_SUPPORTED|CFG_SCM_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Defines if System Clock Manager is used. This module manages clocks and power configuration in order to reach best power figures. The system clock configuration will be updated dynamicaly, so for IP we recommend to use stable clock like HSI clock source.
CFG_SCM_TIMER|CFG_SCM_TIMER|Application configuration - Low Power||||Activate Timer16 or Timer17 in order to allow SCM module to perform timing measurements.
SCM_TIMER_PRIORITY|SCM_TIMER_PRIORITY|Application configuration - Low Power||||SCM_TIMER_PRIORITY must be between RADIO_INTR_PRIO_LOW+1 and RADIO_INTR_PRIO_HIGH-1
CFG_LPM_LEVEL|CFG_LPM_LEVEL|Application configuration - Low Power||||Low Power Module level selection : - 0 : Low Power Mode is not activated, RUN mode will be used. - 1 : Low power active, the one selected with CFG_LPM_STANDBY_SUPPORTED - 2 : In addition log and debug are disabled to reach lowest power figures.
CFG_LPM_STOP1_SUPPORTED|CFG_LPM_STOP1_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Enables support of stop1 mode.
CFG_LPM_STOP2_SUPPORTED|CFG_LPM_STOP2_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Enables support of stop2 mode.
HW_STOP2_SUPPORTED|HW_STOP2_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||HW support of stop2 mode.
HW_STOP3_SUPPORTED|HW_STOP3_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||HW support of stop3 mode.
HW_DIE_WBA5|HW_DIE_WBA5|Application configuration - Low Power||||
HW_DIE_WBA6|HW_DIE_WBA6|Application configuration - Low Power||||
HW_DIE_WBA2|HW_DIE_WBA2|Application configuration - Low Power||||
CFG_LPM_STANDBY_SUPPORTED|CFG_LPM_STANDBY_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Enables support of standby mode.
CFG_LPM_ENHANCED|CFG_LPM_ENHANCED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Enables support of enhanced Low Power Manager.
CFG_LPM_WAKEUP_TIME_PROFILING|CFG_LPM_WAKEUP_TIME_PROFILING|Application configuration - Low Power||||Defines to use dynamic low power wakeup time profilling. With this option at boot wake up time is profiled and then is used.
CFG_LPM_STDBY_WAKEUP_TIME|CFG_LPM_STDBY_WAKEUP_TIME|Application configuration - Low Power||100|10000|Defines time to wake up from standby or stop2 before radio event to meet timings.
CFG_BLE_TM_PROTOCOL|CFG_BLE_TM_PROTOCOL|Application configuration - BLE Transparent Mode||||Transport used for the BLE Transparent Mode communication
BLE_TRANSPARENT_MODE_UART|BLE_TRANSPARENT_MODE_UART|Application configuration - Traces||||Enable or disable communication with STM32CubeWise - Bluetooth LE Explorer
CFG_LOG_SUPPORTED|CFG_LOG_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Logs||||Enable or disable Logs UART print.
