RADIO_INTR_PRIO_LOW|RADIO_INTR_PRIO_LOW|Application configuration - Radio||=(RADIO_INTR_PRIO_HIGH +1)|30|2.4GHz RADIO interrupt priority when radio is Not Active - Sleep Timer Only. Its value must not be inferior to RADIO_INTR_PRIO_HIGH value
RADIO_SW_LOW_INTR_NUM|RADIO_SW_LOW_INTR_NUM|Application configuration - Radio||||Selected interrupt vector for 2.4GHz RADIO low ISR. Possible interrupt vector is part of the list if corresponding IP is not used
RADIO_SW_LOW_INTR_PRIO|RADIO_SW_LOW_INTR_PRIO|Application configuration - Radio||=(RADIO_INTR_PRIO_LOW + 1)|31|2.4GHz RADIO low ISR priority. Its value must not be inferior to RADIO_INTR_PRIO_LOW value
CFG_EXTERNAL_PA_ENABLE|CFG_EXTERNAL_PA_ENABLE|Application configuration - Radio||||External PA activation parameter.
CFG_RF_TX_POWER_TABLE_ID|CFG_RF_TX_POWER_TABLE_ID|Application configuration - Radio||||RF TX power table ID selection: 0 -> RF TX output level from -20 dBm to +10 dBm, with VDDRFPA at VDD level. 1 -> RF TX output level from -20 dBm to +3 dBm, with VDDRFPA at VDD11 level like on ST MB1803 and MB2130 boards. 2 -> RF TX output level at +20 dBm with an external PA, for Transparent Mode only 3 -> RF TX output level from -20 dBm to +3 dBm, only with STOP3 support
CFG_AOA_AOD_ENABLE|CFG_AOA_AOD_ENABLE|Application configuration - Radio||||AOA AOD activation parameter.
CFG_RADIO_NUM_OF_ANTENNAS|CFG_RADIO_NUM_OF_ANTENNAS|Application configuration - Radio||=1|8|Number of antennas for AOA AOD feature.
