SERVICE0_UUID|UUID|Service||||Contains the UUID (only 2 bytes are defined by the user for 16 or 128 bits UUID)
SERVICE0_LONG_NAME|Service long name|Service||||Default value for this SIG Characteristic is: ImmediateAlert
SERVICE0_SHORT_NAME|Service short name|Service||||Default value for this SIG Characteristic is: IAS
SERVICE0_TYPE|Type|Service||||Type of service, either Primary or Secondary
SERVICE0_MAX_ATTRIBUTES_RECORDS|Service max attributes record(s)|Service||||Value depends of the number of characteristics (nbOfChar) with the property Notify or Indicate(nbOfDescriptor) Max_Attributes_Records = 1 + 2*nbOfChar + nbOfDescriptor
SERVICE0_NUMBER_OF_CHARACTERISTICS|Number of characteristics|Service||0|25|Number of services; maximum is 25
SERVICE0_CHAR0|Characteristic|Characteristic0||||characteristic number
SERVICE0_CHAR0_UUID_TYPE|UUID type|Characteristic0||||Type of characteristic UUID, 0x01 = 16 bits UUID, 0x02 = 128 bits UUID
SERVICE0_CHAR0_UUID_ALLOCATION_TYPE|UUID allocation type|Characteristic0||||Type of service UUID, 0x01 = 16 bits UUID, 0x02 = 128 bits UUID
SERVICE0_CHAR0_UUID_128_INPUT_TYPE|UUID 128 input type|Characteristic0||||Characteristic UUID input type, full or reduced
SERVICE0_CHAR0_UUID|UUID|Characteristic0||||Contains the UUID (only 2 bytes are defined by the user for 16 or 128 bits UUID)
SERVICE0_CHAR0_LONG_NAME|Characteristic long name|Characteristic0||||Default value for this SIG Characteristic is: AerobicHeartRateLowerLimit
SERVICE0_CHAR0_SHORT_NAME|Characteristic short name|Characteristic0||||Default value for this SIG Characteristic is: AHRLL
SERVICE0_CHAR0_VALUE_LENGTH|Value length|Characteristic0||1|1024|Number of bytes to be written or to notify (1 to 512). Default value for this SIG Characteristic is: 1
SERVICE0_CHAR0_LENGTH_CHARACTERISTIC|Lenght characteristic|Characteristic0||||Type of characteristic length in ble_defs.h. can be either CHAR_VALUE_LEN_CONSTANT(0x00) or CHAR_VALUE_LEN_VARIABLE(0x01). Default value for this SIG Characteristic is Constant.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ENC_KEY_SIZE|Encryption Key Size|Characteristic0||0x07|0x10|
SERVICE0_CHAR0_PROP_BROADCAST|CHAR_PROP_BROADCAST|Characteristic0||||Broadcasting of the characteristic value using a characteristic configuration descriptor. Default value is No.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_PROP_READ|CHAR_PROP_READ|Characteristic0||||Reading of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_PROP_WRITE_WITHOUT_RESP|CHAR_PROP_WRITE_WITHOUT_RESP|Characteristic0||||Writing Without Response of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_PROP_WRITE|CHAR_PROP_WRITE|Characteristic0||||Write of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_PROP_NOTIFY|CHAR_PROP_NOTIFY|Characteristic0||||Notify of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_PROP_INDICATE|CHAR_PROP_INDICATE|Characteristic0||||Indicate of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_VALUE_OFFSET|Update char value offset|Characteristic0||0|=(SERVICE0_CHAR0_VALUE_LENGTH-1)|The offset from which the attribute value has to be updated. Only active when CHAR_PROP_NOTIFY or CHAR_PROP_INDICATE is selected. Used in custom_stm.c aci_gatt_update_char_value function
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHEN_READ|ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHEN_READ|Characteristic0||||Authentication read of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHOR_READ|ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHOR_READ|Characteristic0||||Authorization read of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ATTR_PERMISSION_ENCRY_READ|ATTR_PERMISSION_ENCRY_READ|Characteristic0||||Encryption read of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHEN_WRITE|ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHEN_WRITE|Characteristic0||||Authentication write of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHOR_WRITE|ATTR_PERMISSION_AUTHOR_WRITE|Characteristic0||||Authorization write of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_ATTR_PERMISSION_ENCRY_WRITE|ATTR_PERMISSION_ENCRY_WRITE|Characteristic0||||Encryption write of the characteristic value. Default value for this SIG characteristic is Yes.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_GATT_NOTIFY_ATTRIBUTE_WRITE|GATT_NOTIFY_ATTRIBUTE_WRITE|Characteristic0||||The application will be notified when a client writes to this attribute. An ACI_GATT_ATTRIBUTE_MODIFIED_EVENT will be issued.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_GATT_NOTIFY_WRITE_REQ_AND_WAIT_FOR_APPL_RESP|GATT_NOTIFY_WRITE_REQ_AND_WAIT_FOR_APPL_RESP|Characteristic0||||The application will be notified when a write request, a write cmd or a signed write cmd is received by the server for this attribute. An ACI_GATT_WRITE_PERMIT_REQ_EVENT will be issued.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_GATT_NOTIFY_READ_REQ_AND_WAIT_FOR_APPL_RESP|GATT_NOTIFY_READ_REQ_AND_WAIT_FOR_APPL_RESP|Characteristic0||||The application will be notified when a read request of any type is received for this attribute. An ACI_GATT_READ_PERMIT_REQ_EVENT will be issued.
SERVICE0_CHAR0_GATT_NOTIFY_NOTIFICATION_COMPLETION|GATT_NOTIFY_NOTIFICATION_COMPLETION|Characteristic0||||The application will be notified when notifications are transmitted. An ACI_GATT_NOTIFICATION_COMPLETE_EVENT will be issued.
mac_802_15_4|mac_802_15_4|mac_802_15_4 application type||||
mac_802_15_4_SKELETON|mac_802_15_4_SKELETON|mac_802_15_4 application type||||
THREAD|THREAD|THREAD application type||||
THREAD_SKELETON|THREAD_SKELETON|THREAD application type||||
THREAD_APPLICATION|Thread Application|THREAD application type||||List of applications types, can be: - Thread_Coap_GenericFull Thread Device(FTD) - Minimal Thread Device(MTD) - Thread Radio Co-Processor(RCP)
THREAD_SKELETON_APPLICATION|Thread Skeleton type|THREAD Skeleton type||||List of applications types, can be: - Full Thread Device(FTD) - Minimal Thread Device(MTD)
CFG_CLI_SUPPORTED|CFG_CLI_SUPPORTED|Parameters||||Enable or disable Thread Command Line Interface.
CFG_THREAD_NETWORK_CONFIG|CFG_THREAD_NETWORK_CONFIG|Parameters||||Enable or disable Thread Network Configuration.
PANID|PANID|Parameters||||Personal Area Network Identifier (PAN ID): an unsigned 16-bit value that specifies the PAN ID. <font color="E6007E"><b>WARNING!: </b></font>The PAN ID MUST be different from 0xFFFF value which is reserved for broadcast PAN ID <b>Value range : </b>0x0 to 0xFFFE
CHANNEL|CHANNEL|Parameters||11|26|2.4 GHz channel as defined in Section 6.1.2.1 of [IEEE802154]
NETWORKKEY|NETWORKKEY|Parameters||||Thread network key
ZIGBEE|ZIGBEE|ZIGBEE Setting||||
ZIGBEE_SKELETON|ZIGBEE_SKELETON|ZIGBEE Setting||||
ZGB_RELEASE|Zigbee Library Release|ZIGBEE Setting||||Zigbee Library Release. Can be R22, R22-SE (FFD only), R23 or R23-ZDD.
ZGB_APPLICATION|Zigbee Application|ZIGBEE Setting||||List of Zigbee application type, can be: - Full Function Device (FFD) - Reduced Function Device with only End Device and Sleepy End Device available for lower energy consumption(RFD)
ZIGBEE_SKELETON_APPLICATION|Zigbee skeleton|ZIGBEE Skeleton type||||List of Zigbee Skeleton type, can be: - Skeleton Full Function Device (FFD) - Skeleton Reduced Function Device with only End Device and Sleepy End Device available for lower energy consumption(RFD)
ZGB_NW_MODE|Zigbee Network Mode|ZIGBEE Setting||||Network configuration, can be: - Centralized - Distributed - Touchlink
ZGB_DEVICE_ROLE|Zigbee Device Role|ZIGBEE Setting||||List of application type, can be: - Coordinator (for FFD application only) - Router (for FFD application only) - End Device - Sleepy End Device
ZGB_TOUCHLINK_CAPABILITY|Touchlink capability|ZIGBEE Setting||||Touchlink device can handle 2 capabilities in RFD application: - Router - End device, which allows Sleepy mode
ZGB_SLEEPY_MODE|Sleepy mode|ZIGBEE Setting||||Sleepy mode is available in RFD applications, except in Touchlink mode for router capability. It turns on the low power mode parameters.
ZGB_ADV_SETTTING_TYPE|Advanced Setting Type|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||||Type of Advanced Setting.
ZGB_ADV_PARAM_TYPE|Advanced Setting Type|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||||Type of Advanced Setting.
ZGB_ADV_SETTTING_PREDEF|Predefined Settings|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||||Predefined Setting : Home (10-100 Devices), Building (50-500 Devices) and Industial (100-1000+ Devices).
ZGB_APS_BINDING_TBL_SZ|APS Binding Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||1|255|Number of entries in the APS Binding Table. Default FFD value is 64.
ZGB_APS_GROUP_TBL_SZ|APS Group Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||1|253|Number of entries in the APS Group Table. Default FFD value is 16.
ZGB_APS_LINK_KEY_TBL_SZ|APS Key Link Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||1|255|Number of entries in the APS Key Link Table. Default FFD value is 32.
ZGB_NWK_NEIGHBOR_TBL_SZ|Network Neighbor Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||1|255|Number of entries in the Network Neighbor Table. Default FFD value is 64.
ZGB_NWK_ROUTE_TBL_SZ|Network Route Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||0|0|Number of entries in the Network Route Table. Default FFD value is 32.
ZGB_NWK_ADDR_MAP_TBL_SZ|Network Address Map Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||1|255|Number of entries in the Network Address Map Table. Default FFD value is 32.
ZGB_NWK_BTT_TBL_SZ|Network Broadcast Transaction Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||1|255|Number of entries in the Network Broadcast Transaction Table. Default FFD value is 32.
ZGB_NWK_RREQ_TBL_SZ|Network Route Request Table Entries|ZIGBEE Advanced Setting||0|255|Number of entries in the Network Route Request Table. Default FFD value is 16.
ZGB_TCSO_TYPE|Zigbee Trust Center Type|ZIGBEE Trust Center||||Zigbee Trust Center Type. Can be None, Server or Client. Only for R22-SE or R23.
ZGB_NB_ENDPOINTS|Number of End Points|End Points||1|10|Number of endpoints used on one device. At least one endpoint is mandatory for a Zigbee application, and it should not exceed 10.
ZGB_CHANNEL_SELECT|Channel Selection|Network Parameters||||Channel Selection : One channel or Channel Mask.
ZGB_CHANNEL|Channel|Network Parameters||0|26|Network channel should be set between 0 and 26.
ZGB_CHANNEL_MASK|Channel Mask|Network Parameters||0x0800|0x07FFF800|Network Channel Mask should be set between 0x800 and 0x07FFF800.
ZGB_CHANNEL_PREDEF|Predefined Channel Mask|Network Parameters||||Network Channel Mask already defined in Zigbee Stack.
ZGB_PERSISTENCE|Zigbee Persistence|ZIGBEE Persistence||||Zigbee Persistence. Two possibles backup types : with an Eeprom Emulator or with the SNVMA.
ZGB_OTA|OTA Cluster Type|ZIGBEE Firmware Update Over The Air (OTA)||||Zigbee Firmware Update Over The Air. None, OTA Server or OTA Client.
ZGB_OTA_ENDPOINT|OTA Endpoint|ZIGBEE Firmware Update Over The Air (OTA)||1|240|Endpoint for OTA beetween 1 to 240.
ZGB_OTA_PROFILE|OTA Profile ID|ZIGBEE Firmware Update Over The Air (OTA)||||Profile ID for OTA.
ENDPOINT0_ID_ZGB|Endpoint ID|Endpoint||1|240|Endpoint <b>242</b> shall be reserved for the <b>Green Power cluster</b>, used in proxy mode with FFD application and not used with RFD application. <font color="E6007E"><b>WARNING:</b> Endpoint IDs shall be <b>unique</b> in one same device.
ZGB_ENDPOINT0_PROFILE_ID|Profile ID|Endpoint||||Profile of the endpoint, can be: - Home Automation (HA) - Zigbee Light Link (ZLL)
ZGB_ENDPOINT0_DEVICE_ID|Device ID|Endpoint||||Device description gives a readable information about the application of the device
ZGB_ENDPOINT0_GROUP_ADDRESS_ACTIVATION|Group Address activation|Endpoint||||No GROUP_ADDRESS for an End Device
ZGB_ENDPOINT0_GROUP_ADDRESS|Group Address|Endpoint||||GROUP_ADDRESS value
ZCL_BASIC_ENDPOINT0|Basic|Clusters||||Basic cluster: server mode mandatory for all Zigbee endpoint.
ZCL_IDENTIFY_ENDPOINT0|Identify|Clusters||||Identify cluster allows to be in identification mode. - Server receives commands to start and stop identification mode. - Client sends start and stop commands to the server.
ZCL_ALARM_ENDPOINT0|Alarms|Clusters||||Alarm cluster configure alarm functionality and send alarm notifications. - Server resides with other clusters which can generate alarm conditions and it sends them to a cluster client. Time server cluster SHALL be set when Alarms server is used. - Client can send user instructions to the server.
ZCL_TIME_ENDPOINT0|Time|Clusters||||Time cluster provides a base for real-time application. - Server acts as a time master for the network. It SHALL be set when Alarm server or DRLC client are used. - Client synchronizes itself with the server.
ZCL_COMMISSIONING_ENDPOINT0|Commissioning|Clusters||||Commissioning cluster allows a commissioning process. - Server responds to a commissioning process and commissions itself into a network. - Client initiates the commissioning of a commissioning server.
ZCL_GROUPS_ENDPOINT0|Groups|Clusters||||Groups cluster manages group addressing. - Server receives configuration commands regarding to the local group table. - Client sends commands to configure the group table.
ZCL_SCENES_ENDPOINT0|Scenes|Clusters||||Scenes cluster allows to configure a set of stored values to create recalling scenes. - Server receives commands to configure scenes. - Client controls the configuration of the scenes.
ZCL_OCCUPANCY_SENSING_ENDPOINT0|Occupancy Sensing|Clusters||||Occupancy Sensing cluster provides an interface to an occupancy sensor. - Server receives commands to configure the sensor and reports to the client. - Client sends commands to configure the sensor and receives report from the sensor.
ZCL_DIAGNOSTICS_ENDPOINT0|Diagnostics|Clusters||||Diagnostic cluster informs about the operation of the stack over time and will be used by multiple profiles. As a result it should not be set alone. - Server provides diagnostic data. Attributes are strongly recommended to be stored in persistent memory. - Client sends requests to access diagnostic data.
ZCL_POLL_CONTROL_ENDPOINT0|Poll Control|Clusters||||Poll Control cluster provides a mechanism for the management of a Zigbee End Device's polling mode.It defines the poll interval between (normal or fast) two MAC Data Requests from the ZED to its parent router. - Server sets the polling mode to Normal (long poll interval) or Fast (short poll interval) after periodically checking the client. - Client decides the polling mode to be selected.
ZCL_POWER_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT0|Power Configuration|Clusters||||Power Configuration cluster provides information about the power source and voltage alarms to be configured. - Server receives commands to set its power configuration. - Client sends commands to set the power configuration on a remote device.
ZCL_POWER_PROFILE_ENDPOINT0|Power Profile|Clusters||||Power Profile cluster indicates the expected power profile to a controller. - Server provides the local power profile. - Client receives the power profile.
ZCL_RSSI_LOCATION_ENDPOINT0|RSSI Location|Clusters||||RSSI Location cluster allows exchanges of Received Signal Strength Indication information. - Server requests RSSI information and report RSSI measurement. - Client answers to the server requests and reports.
ZCL_PRESSURE_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT0|Pressure Measurement|Clusters||||Pressure Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control pressure measurement. - Server measures the pressure. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_DEVICE_TEMPERATURE_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT0|Device Temperature Configuration|Clusters||||Device Temperature Configuration cluster measures internal temperature and configures temperature alarms. - Server receives commands to access internal temperature data. - Client sends commands to access the internal temperature.
ZCL_TEMPERATURE_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT0|Temperature Measurement|Clusters||||Temperature Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control temperature measurements. - Server measures the temperature. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_THERMOSTAT_ENDPOINT0|Thermostat Configuration|Clusters||||Thermostat cluster provides an interface to configure and control a thermostat. - Server configures the thermostat. - Client controls the functionalities of the thermostat.
ZCL_THERMOSTAT_UI_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT0|Thermostat User Interface Configuration|Clusters||||Thermostat UI Configuration cluster provides an interface to configure the user interface of a thermostat. - Server configures the thermostat UI. - Client controls the functionalities of the thermostat UI.
ZCL_METER_IDENTIFICATION_ENDPOINT0|Meter Identification|Clusters||||Meter Identification cluster determines advanced information about utility metering device. - Server provides information. - Client sends requests to the server for information.
ZCL_ELECTRICALMEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT0|Electrical Measurement|Clusters||||Electrical Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control electrical measurements. - Server makes the electrical measurements. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_FAN_CONTROL_ENDPOINT0|Fan Control|Clusters||||Fan Control cluster controls the speed and state of a fan. - Server configures the speed or state of the fan. - Client commands the server to set the speed or state of the fan.
ZCL_PUMP_CONFIGURATION_CONTROL_ENDPOINT0|Pump Configuration and Control|Clusters||||Pump Configuration and Control cluster provides an interface to configure and control pump devices (control of speed not included). - Server configures the pump. - Client controls the functionalities of the pump.
ZCL_WATER_CONTENT_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT0|Water Content Measurement|Clusters||||Water Content Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control humidity measurements. - Server measures the humidity. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_ONOFF_ENDPOINT0|On/Off|Clusters||||On/Off cluster provides functionality to switch a device between On and Off states. - Server receives commands to change the state. Server mode SHALL be set if Level Control cluster OR if Color Control are in server mode. - Client sends commands to request a change of state.
ZCL_COLORCONTROL_ENDPOINT0|Color Control|Clusters||||Color Control cluster controls the color of a light. - Server receives commands to change the color of the light. - Client sends commands to change the color of the remote light.
ZCL_ILLUMINANCE_LEVEL_SENSING_ENDPOINT0|Illuminance Level Sensing|Clusters||||Illuminance Level Sensing cluster provides an interface to configure and control level of illumination watch. - Server senses the level of illumination. - Client configures and gets the notifications from the server.
ZCL_ILLUMINANCE_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT0|Illuminance Measurement|Clusters||||Illuminance Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control illuminance measurements. - Server measures the illuminance and report to the client. - Client configures the server and control receives measurements from it.
ZCL_LEVELCONTROL_ENDPOINT0|Level Control|Clusters||||Level Control cluster controls the level of a characteristic value of a device. - Server receives commands to change the level of characteristic values. OnOff server SHALL be set when Level Control server is used. - Client sends commands to change the level of characteristic values.
ZCL_ON_OFF_SWITCH_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT0|On/Off Switch Configuration|Clusters||||On/Off Switch Configuration cluster provides the switch type on a device. - Server receives commands to define a switch configuration. - Client sends commands to define a switch configuration.
ZCL_DOOR_LOCK_ENDPOINT0|Door Lock|Clusters||||Door Lock cluster provides an interface to configure and control generic values of door locks and doors. - Server sets the values representing door security. - Client controls the door lock and the door.
ZCL_WINDOW_COVERING_ENDPOINT0|Window Covering|Clusters||||Window Covering cluster provides an interface to configure and control window coverings. - Server sets the values of the window covering. - Client controls the window covering.
ZCL_IAS_ACE_ENDPOINT0|IAS Ancillary Control Equipment (ACE)|Clusters||||IAS ACE cluster provides an interface to configure and control a Control and Indicating Equipment (CIE) in an Intruder Alarm System (IAS). - Server receives commands to configure the CIE. - Client sends commands to configure and control the CIE.
ZCL_IAS_WD_ENDPOINT0|IAS Warning Device (WD)|Clusters||||IAS WD cluster provides an interface to configure and control a Warning Device (WD) in an Intruder Alarm System (IAS). - Server receives commands to configure the WD and report to the client. - Client sends commands to configure and control the WD and receives reports.
ZCL_IAS_ZONE_ENDPOINT0|IAS Zone|Clusters||||IAS Zone cluster provides an interface to configure and control an IAS security zone device. - Server receives commands to configure the IAS Zone device and report to the client. - Client sends commands to configure and control the IAS Zone device and receives reports.
ZCL_MESSAGING_ENDPOINT0|Messaging|SE Clusters||||Messaging cluster an interface to pass text messages from one device to another. - Server sends the text message. - Client receives the text message.
ZCL_DRLC_ENDPOINT0|Demand Response and Load Control|SE Clusters||||DRLC cluster provides an interface to the functionality of Demand Response and Load Control. - Server sends the Load Control Events to the devices. - Client receives the Load Control Events. It is time-dependent, therefore a Time server cluster SHALL be set when DRLC client is used.
ZCL_METERING_ENDPOINT0|Metering|SE Clusters||||Metering cluster provides an interface to obtain usage information from metering devices. - Server gives information. - Client asks for usage information to the server.
ZCL_PRICE_ENDPOINT0|Price|SE Clusters||||Price cluster provides an interface to communicates pricing information. - Server gives price information. - Client asks for price information to the server.
ZCL_TUNNELING_ENDPOINT0|Smart Energy Tunneling|SE Clusters||||Smart Energy Tunneling cluster provides an interface for tunneling protocols. - Server provides and manages tunnels. - Client requests a tunnel and close it.
ZCL_KEY_ESTABLISHMENT_ENDPOINT0|Key Establishment|SE Clusters||||Key Establishment cluster is to be used for communication between devices if original network security can not be trusted. - Server initiates the secure communication transaction. - Client responds the secure communication transation.
ZCL_DEHUMIDIFICATION_CONTROL_ENDPOINT0|Dehumidification Control|Clusters||||Dehumidification Control cluster provides an interface to configure an control dehumidification devices. - Server configures the dehumidification device. - Client controls the functionalities of the dehumidification device.
ZCL_BALLAST_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT0|Ballast Configuration|Clusters||||Ballast Configuration cluster provides an interface to configure an control lighting ballasts. - Server receives command to configure the lighting ballasts. - Client sends commands to configure and control lighting ballasts.
ZCL_NEAREST_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT0|Nearest Gateway|Clusters||||Nearest Gateway cluster provides an interface to send nearest gateway information. - Server gives the information of nearest gateway. - Client asks for the nearest gateway.
ZCL_OTA_UPGRADE_ENDPOINT0|OTA Upgrade|Specific Clusters||||OTA Upgrade cluster allows to upgrade application software over the air. - Server distributes the software to upgrade. - Client receives the software to update.
ZCL_VOICE_OVER_ZGB_ENDPOINT0|Voice Over Zigbee|Specific Clusters||||Voice Over Zigbee cluster allows voice transmition between Zigbee devices. - Server receives the voice message. - Client sends the voice message.
